"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Favorable findings include negative surgical margins and the absence of seminal vesicle invasion, which are positive prognostic indicators. The absence of lymphovascular invasion is also noted. Conversely, the preoperative PSA of 6.4 and the pathological stage of pT3a contribute to a less favorable baseline. The absence of documented nodal sampling widens the uncertainty regarding nodal status, as pNx is not equivalent to pN0. The biopsy finding of Gleason 3+5 in the transition zone differs from the prostatectomy specimen, which is a point of divergence in the documented findings. Postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory are critical missing pieces of information that would significantly revise this assessment. The current heuristic horizon suggests a follow-up period of approximately 40 months without an event. The fixed estimated horizon is 40.44 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 26.29–54.59 months; its coverage has not been validated."
